{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>שמע ישראל ה' אלהינו ה' אחד</b> — What our ancients of blessed memory transmitted regarding the Shema is the truth, and there is no need to seek [other] opinions. Know that this esteemed Name is a noun of substance, and if so, what reason is there to say it a second time? The answer: <b>אדם</b> is both a noun of substance and a noun of accident — and it is not so here [i.e. with the divine Name]. If <b>אדם</b> is called from the substance of earth (<i>מעצם האדמה</i>), so too here [<b>אלהינו</b>]. And the proof is the Name that is joined to צבאות, or the principal [name] is <b>אלהינו</b>, and it is doubled likewise to say <b>אחד</b>, and the reason is 'alone.' And there are proofs beyond number that the Name is one, as in the verse: <i>In that day YHWH will be one</i> (Zechariah 14:9) — upon human thought. And what seems correct to me is that it is joined with 'king,' for thus it is written: <i>YHWH will be king over all the earth</i> (ibid.) — <i>In that day YHWH will be one king and His name one</i> — in the sense of <i>then I will turn to the peoples a clear language</i> (Zephaniah 3:9), and behold all the world will speak one language; therefore the name of YHWH will be one."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The text is heavily compressed and reads at points like corrupt or defective copy; I have translated hyper-literally without smoothing. 'Upon human thought' (על מחשבות בני אדם) is obscure as it stands and may be defective. The argument about אדם and מעצם האדמה is elliptical in the original and left so."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:39.256994522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}